      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:3:34:3",
      "text": [
        " إِذَا أَقَرَّ الرَّجُلُ عَلَى نَفْسِهِ بِحَدٍّ أَوْ فِرْيَةٍ ثُمَّ جَحَدَ جُلِدَ قُلْتُ أَ رَأَيْتَ إِنْ أَقَرَّ بِحَدٍّ عَلَى نَفْسِهِ يَبْلُغُ فِيهِ الرَّجْمَ أَ كُنْتَ تَرْجُمُهُ قَالَ لَا وَ لَكِنْ كُنْتُ ضَارِبَهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hammad Bin Usman, from Al Halby, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘When the man accepts upon himself with a Penalty (Hadd), or fabrication, then denies it, would be whipped’. I said, ‘What is your view that if he accepts with a Penalty (<span class=\"iTxt\">Hadd</span>) upon himself, in which stoning is reached, would you<sup>asws</sup> have him stoned?’ He <sup>asws</sup> said: ‘No. But, I<sup>asws</sup> would have whipped him’."
        ]
      }
    },
